    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d353">

                <pb facs="0367" n="251" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg251"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.00/641.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1912-05-29T21:00:00-05:29">
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">May</hi> 29, 1912—9 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In pursuance of your May 29, I saw the President, who declared that he recognized
                    our rights under the circumstances named. He added emphatic appreciation of our
                    Government’s “fine attitude” throughout present crisis, which he says has been
                    worth more to him than his entire army.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Beaupré</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
